/-!
# Finiteness of the associated points of a Noetherian scheme

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 05AF, `lemma-finite-ass`, specialized to the
structure sheaf and the quasi-compact open consisting of the whole scheme
(blueprint: lem-sfb-noetherian-associated-points-finite).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The associated points of a quasi-compact locally Noetherian scheme form a finite set.
The empty scheme is included.

Source: Stacks Project, Divisors, Tag 05AF, `lemma-finite-ass`, with the affine
translation of Tag 02OK and Algebra Tags 00LC and 0310 (2)
(blueprint: lem-sfb-noetherian-associated-points-finite).

Proof:
1. By `pqf-def-locnoeth`, take an affine open cover with Noetherian coordinate rings.
   Quasi-compactness gives a finite subcover. Every prime of each coordinate ring is
   finitely generated, by `def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring`.
2. Each coordinate ring is finite as a module over itself, generated by 1. Thus
   `lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-associated-primes-finite` (`associatedPrimes.finite`) makes
   its set of associated primes finite.
3. For an associated point in one of these affine opens, use
   `lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization` to identify its stalk with the
   localization of the coordinate ring at its corresponding prime. The stalk is
   Noetherian, so the predicate in `def-sc-associated-points` means that its maximal
   ideal is an actual annihilator, by `isAssociatedPrime_iff`. A ring isomorphism
   preserves maximal ideals and annihilators. Apply `lem-sc-associated-localization-fg`
   to descend this annihilator from the localization to the coordinate ring. The
   point therefore lies in the image of that ring's finite associated-prime set.
4. Every associated point lies in one of the finitely many affine opens. Their finite
   associated-prime images have finite union, and `associatedPoints X` is a subset
   of this union. For the empty scheme the associated-point set is empty. -/
theorem finite_associatedPoints (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [CompactSpace X] :
    (associatedPoints X).Finite := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
